**定义 76.4（rational periodic, zero and evidence words）。** A rational field represents $z/d$ by gamma($\zeta(z)$) and gamma($d-1$), with $d\geq1$. A periodic word contains nine such fields, with no trailing data. They are the three row vectors in phase order $(x_3,x_1,x_2)$. The decoder returns the row selected by $j\bmod3$. An exact rational instrument supplies finite numerator and denominator strings for the same actual three reads; it checks their arity and their squared norms by finite rational arithmetic. If the two later squared norms are both exactly one, the actual-source promise gives the neutral branch. Compute the signed cross product $x_3$ by the division-free closure and store these exact periodic rows. Every denominator width and every rational output width is paid. A finite exact comparison of rational fields is not a test for equality of arbitrary real names.

With a separately truthful neutral certificate $q_1=q_2=1$, request the archive at $b=2K+24$, set $p=K+10$, compute the sign-corrected cross product from the finite replies, and round all coordinates of the three periodic rows to the nearest $2^{-p}$ grid. Store those reduced dyadic rationals with this periodic grammar. The error estimates in §79 yield the prescribed uniform error with $O(K)$ numerical bits. The certificate and its issuance are additional charges. For $D>0$, the exact rational instrument instead forms dyadic replies by nearest-coordinate rounding at each requested precision and uses §79; three coordinate errors of at most $2^{-b-1}$ have Euclidean norm less than $2^{-b}$, so they are valid names. It pays the actual original rational widths and the requested production work.

The exact-zero word is exactly its mode, with no data. Its semantic authority is an actual zero-future source or a separately truthful zero-regime certificate; a syntactically recognized zero word is not that certificate. It returns three zero numerators at precision zero for every valid future query. A wrapper is one wrapper mode, gamma($M$), exactly $M$ binary evidence bits, then one core loss, periodic, zero or orientation word. Truncated evidence and nonbinary evidence are invalid. Wrappers do not recursively certify their own truth or introduce an archive into the core. The full additional length is $8+2\lfloor\log_2(M+1)\rfloor+1+M$. A mandatory transcript, source identity or proof certificate is retained literally when the interface requires it; its length has no asserted numerical-core bound.

